1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,680
AI can hand a child a confident answer in seconds.

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:07,680
The harder skill is the pause before believing it.

3
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:12,880
Before you believe it turns that pause into a five-minute ritual a parent and child do

4
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,880
together.

5
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:15,800
A parent enters any topic.

6
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:19,840
Here, electric cars are better for the planet and an age band.

7
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:22,879
The child's own answer never leaves the browser.

8
00:00:22,879 --> 00:00:29,200
GPT 5.6, through the OpenAI Responses API, builds a complete reasoning mission in real-time,

9
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:33,599
a claim, the questions worth pausing on, the hidden assumptions, balanced evidence

10
00:00:33,599 --> 00:00:35,860
clues, and answer starters.

11
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:37,299
This is a real request.

12
00:00:37,299 --> 00:00:39,360
The wait is never faked.

13
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:41,400
Every step now explores that topic.

14
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:44,599
First, the child picks the question that makes them pause.

15
00:00:44,599 --> 00:00:49,520
Pushback reveals a hidden assumption inside the claim, the word always doing too much

16
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:50,520
work.

17
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:54,759
Check sets the claim beside evidence clues, not a verdict, and asks what would change

18
00:00:54,759 --> 00:00:55,959
their mind.

19
00:00:55,959 --> 00:00:58,880
Make lets the child build an answer in their own words.

20
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:02,000
The AI never grades, scores, or ranks it.

21
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,320
OWN prints a learning receipt that keeps four things separate — what the child bought,

22
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:10,320
what AI helped with, what they checked, and what is still uncertain.

23
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:15,519
I built this with OpenAI Codex, the accessible canvas, the deterministic mission state and

24
00:01:15,519 --> 00:01:21,139
receipt, the signed judge access boundary, the GPT 5.6 schema validation, and the full

25
00:01:21,139 --> 00:01:22,320
test suite.

26
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:25,300
GPT 5.6 is the live engine.

27
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:30,839
Every topic reshapes the whole mission, behind server-side access and strict schema validation.

28
00:01:30,839 --> 00:01:33,459
And the child's answer is never sent to the model.

29
00:01:33,459 --> 00:01:35,940
AI prepares the material to question.

30
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:37,580
The family does the reasoning.

31
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:39,419
That's before you believe it.


